extends layout

block content
  if sitekey
    script(src='https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api.js', async, defer)
  .page-header
    h3.text-center #{title}
    hr
    p Note: There is a known user interface bug where the unexpanded drop-down menu (navigation bar) hangs over the title of a given page in this site, covering some of the title. For me this happens when my font size is set to "large" in my phone's settings.
    p Also, there was a known bug where when you try to sign in, the sign in might not work the first time even if you put in the right password. It just redirects you to the homepage without actually signing you in. Just try signing in again using the same password. You might have to try it twice. This bug can occur after creating a new account as well.
    p If you have any other issues, describe them below. The report is emailed to the developer.

    if sitekey
      form.form-horizontal#contactForm(method='POST')
        input(type='hidden', name='_csrf', value=_csrf)
        .form-group.row.justify-content-md-center
          label.col-sm-2.col-form-label.text-right.font-weight-bold(for='name') Name
          .col-sm-8
            input.form-control(type='text', name='name', id='name', maxlength='200', autocomplete='name', autofocus, required)
        .form-group.row.justify-content-md-center
          label.col-sm-2.col-form-label.text-right.font-weight-bold(for='email') Email
          .col-sm-8
            input.form-control(type='email', name='email', id='email', maxlength='320', autocomplete='email', required)
        .form-group.row.justify-content-md-center
          label.col-sm-2.col-form-label.text-right.font-weight-bold(for='message') Issue
          .col-sm-8
            textarea.form-control(name='message', id='message', rows='7', maxlength='4000', required)
        .form-group.row.justify-content-md-center
          .offset-sm-2.col-sm-8
            .g-recaptcha(data-sitekey=sitekey)
            p#recaptchaError.text-danger.d-none.mt-2 Please complete the reCAPTCHA before sending.
            button.btn.btn-primary.mt-3(type='submit')
              i.fa.fa-envelope
              |  Send
      script.
        document.getElementById("contactForm").addEventListener("submit", function (event) {
          var recaptchaError = document.getElementById("recaptchaError");
          if (typeof grecaptcha !== "undefined" && !grecaptcha.getResponse()) {
            event.preventDefault();
            recaptchaError.classList.remove("d-none");
          } else if (recaptchaError) {
            recaptchaError.classList.add("d-none");
          }
        });
    else
      .alert.alert-warning
        | This form cannot send yet. Google reCAPTCHA keys still need to be set on the server.
